			"type": "text",
			"text": "Antarctaspis mcmurdoensis is a species of basal arthrodire from the Middle-Late Devonian aged Aztec Siltstone Formation in Victoria Land, Antarctica. It is known from an incomplete skull measuring 7 centimeters in length. Antarctaspis is one of the most basal arthrodires known. It is the namesake of the controversial Antarctaspidae, a family comprising of some of the most basal arthrodires."
		},
		{
			"advancement": "lepidodendron:pf_adv_book_antarctaspis",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "However, this group is debated, with some seeing it as a group of basal arthrodires with no connection beyond that."
